{"E:\\videos\\tswfilters\\wt\\vlog\\tswsalt\\voz\\b010_t3.wav": {"text": "And when the pot is off, people pull their chairs in around it, because the ground and the steel keep throwing heat for a long time. I left a thermometer in the dirt six inches from the bucket. Before the fire, it read 41 degrees. After an hour of burning, the dirt read 130. That warm ring of ground is why a fire hole keeps your feet warm on a cold night. One more thing I noticed. With the salt, a white crust built up on the sand after an hour, and the drops started to bead up on it instead of soaking in. Without salt, the sand stayed dark and even. So the salt is not just useless for heat. Over a long night, it actually gets in the way. Why does a hole in the dirt burn so clean? Three reasons. The hot sand turns every drop into vapor, because oil burns as a gas, not as a liquid. The air tunnel feeds fresh air straight into the bottom of the fire.", "words": [{"w": " And", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.14}, {"w": " when", "s": 0.14, "e": 0.28}, {"w": " the", "s": 0.28, "e": 0.48}, {"w": " pot", "s": 0.48, "e": 0.7}, {"w": " is", "s": 0.7, "e": 0.9}, {"w": " off,", "s": 0.9, "e": 1.78}, {"w": " people", "s": 1.78, "e": 1.88}, {"w": " pull", "s": 1.88, "e": 2.2}, {"w": " their", "s": 2.2, "e": 2.4}, {"w": " chairs", "s": 2.4, "e": 2.8}, {"w": " in", "s": 2.8, "e": 3.08}, {"w": " around", "s": 3.08, "e": 3.44}, {"w": " it,", "s": 3.44, "e": 4.08}, {"w": " because", "s": 4.08, "e": 4.22}, {"w": " the", "s": 4.22, "e": 4.46}, {"w": " ground", "s": 4.46, "e": 4.92}, {"w": " and", "s": 4.92, "e": 5.14}, {"w": " the", "s": 5.14, "e": 5.26}, {"w": " steel", "s": 5.26, "e": 5.72}, {"w": " keep", "s": 5.72, "e": 6.22}, {"w": " throwing", "s": 6.22, "e": 6.6}, {"w": " heat", "s": 6.6, "e": 6.94}, {"w": " for", "s": 6.94, "e": 7.16}, {"w": " a", "s": 7.16, "e": 7.3}, {"w": " long", "s": 7.3, "e": 7.54}, {"w": " time.", "s": 7.54, "e": 8.44}, {"w": " I", "s": 8.6, "e": 8.7}, {"w": " left", "s": 8.7, "e": 9.0}, {"w": " a